Project: EduNexus

Root:
  ./

Architecture:
  ModularMonolith

Domains:
  Backend
  Frontend
  Mobile
  QA
  DevOps

Flow:
  BE -> FE -> MD -> QA -> DO -> VERIFY

Paths:
  BE: ./backend
  FE: ./frontend
  MD: ./mobile
  QA: ./qa
  DO: ./devops

Specs:
  ./.sdd/project
  (per-module: ./.sdd/project/<module>/ — see project/map.sdd)

Skills:
  BE: ./.sdd/backend
  FE: ./.sdd/frontend
  MD: ./.sdd/mobile
  QA: ./.sdd/qa
  DO: ./.sdd/devops

Chains:
  ./.sdd/chains

Protocol:
  ./.sdd/protocol/symbols.sdd
  ./.sdd/protocol/rules.sdd

Prompts:
  root: ./.sdd/system/MASTER.md
  inbox: ./.sdd/prompts/inbox
  active: ./.sdd/prompts/active
  archive: ./.sdd/prompts/archive
  rejected: ./.sdd/prompts/rejected

Tasks:
  ./.sdd/tasks

Decisions:
  ./.sdd/decisions

Workflow:
  1. ANALYZE
  2. PROPOSE
  3. HUMAN_APPROVAL
  4. PLAN
  5. BACKEND
  6. FRONTEND
  7. MOBILE
  8. QA
  9. DEVOPS
  10. VERIFY

DefaultExecutionChain:
  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

  AN  = Analysis
  AR  = Architecture
  DB  = Database        (optional — see per-module flow.sdd condition)
  BE  = Backend
  API = API
  FE  = Frontend
  MD  = Mobile
  QA  = Quality Assurance
  DO  = DevOps
  VR  = Verify

  Full abbreviation table + optional-stage mechanism: protocol/stages.sdd
  Per-feature execution chain lives in project/<module>/flow.sdd, not here
  (global files stay routing-only — see project/map.sdd).

Rules:
  Human approval required before implementation.
  Failed task must return to the responsible stage (see protocol/rules.sdd).
  Failed review must not automatically skip to next stage.
  QA failure returns to implementation/review according to failure reason.
  DevOps failure returns to DevOps.
  Verification failure creates corrective task.
  Completed stages cannot be silently skipped.
  See protocol/rules.sdd -> RULE: CHAIN_INTEGRITY for the full enforcement contract.

AdaptivePipeline:
  Default pipeline above is not mandatory for every task.
  Each task/feature declares its own "Required stages" subset in its chain file.

  Example — backend-only bugfix:
    BE -> QA -> VERIFY

  Example — UI-only change:
    FE -> MD -> QA -> VERIFY

  Example — infrastructure-only change:
    DO -> VERIFY

Note:
  This is a template/example instance derived from the EduNexus illustration
  used in the source conversation (prompt/new/1.md..8.md). When applied to a
  real project, this file and ./project/* MUST be regenerated from evidence
  per project/architecture.sdd -> ProjectInstantiation, not copied as-is.
